{"step_index":428,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:05:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-18T08:05:58-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-18T08:05:58-06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/djtwo/.gemini/config/skills/rlcf-video-editing/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 63\nTotal Bytes: 3461\nShowing lines 1 to 63\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: rlcf-video-editing\n3: description: Automates processing and editing of RLCF Sunday meeting livestream recordings in DaVinci Resolve. Use when the user wants to process Sunday livestream videos, extract the worship/singing section, section off individual songs, remove singing, or generate YouTube chapter timestamps.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # RLCF Sunday Livestream Video Editing Workflow\n7: \n8: This skill documents the automated workflow for processing weekly River of Life Christian Fellowship (RLCF) Sunday meeting livestream recordings in DaVinci Resolve.\n9: \n10: ## 1. System Environment & File Locations\n11: - **OS**: Windows\n12: - **User Downloads Folder**: `C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads`\n13: - **Video Filename Pattern**: `RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - <Month> <Day>, <Year>.mp4`\n14: - **FFmpeg Path**: `C:\\Program Files\\Presenter\\resources\\ffmpeg\\ffmpeg.exe`\n15: - **Python**: Python 3.14 with `faster-whisper`, `numpy`, `scipy` installed.\n16: - **DaVinci Resolve Scripts Directory**:\n17:   `C:\\Users\\djtwo\\AppData\\Roaming\\Blackmagic Design\\DaVinci Resolve\\Support\\Fusion\\Scripts\\Edit\\`\n18: \n19: ## 2. Standard Service Structure\n20: Every RLCF Sunday Livestream generally follows this structure:\n21: 1. **00:00:00 to ~00:04:30**: Pre-stream holding slide / silence.\n22: 2. **~00:04:30 to ~00:06:15**: Opening spoken greeting & welcome prayer.\n23: 3. **~00:06:15 to ~00:36:15**: **Praise & Worship Set**\n24:    - 5 or 6 worship songs / hymns accompanied by instruments.\n25:    - Spoken prayers, scripture reading, and encouragements between the songs.\n26: 4. **~00:36:15**: Worship concludes; silence gap as speaker approaches the pulpit.\n27: 5. **~00:36:30 onwards**: Announcements, Sunday school memory verses, main sermon, testimonies, and closing prayer.\n28: \n29: ## 3. Workflow Procedures\n30: \n31: ### Step A: Rapid Audio Extraction & Whisper Transcription\n32: Extract 16kHz mono audio from the video:\n33: ```powershell\n34: & \"C:\\Program Files\\Presenter\\resources\\ffmpeg\\ffmpeg.exe\" -y -i \"$videoPath\" -vn -ac 1 -ar 16000 \"$scratchDir\\audio_16k.wav\"\n35: ```\n36: Run `faster-whisper` (`tiny.en` on CPU with `int8` or CUDA) over the first 40 minutes (0 to 2400 seconds) to obtain word-level timestamps and locate:\n37: - Opening prayer end / Song 1 start (exact start of singing).\n38: - Each song's start and end boundaries.\n39: - The end of the worship set (exact end of singing, before announcements).\n40: \n41: ### Step B: DaVinci Resolve Automation (Lua Scripting)\n42: Instead of relying on XML/EDL imports which can run into timecode extent mismatches with MP4s, generate and place a `.lua` script in:\n43: `C:\\Users\\djtwo\\AppData\\Roaming\\Blackmagic Design\\DaVinci Resolve\\Support\\Fusion\\Scripts\\Edit\\`\n44: \n45: The script uses Resolve's native scripting API:\n46: 1. Grabs the imported video clip from the Media Pool.\n47: 2. Determines the clip's `Start TC` offset and `FPS`.\n48: 3. Creates the requested timeline (`CreateEmptyTimeline`).\n49: 4. Uses `mediaPool:AppendToTimeline(clipInfos)` with exact `startFrame` and `endFrame` ranges.\n50: 5. Applies timeline markers with song titles (`timeline:AddMarker`) and color codes clips (Teal for songs, Orange for speaking).\n51: \n52: The user runs the script with one click from:\n53: **Workspace -> Scripts -> Edit -> [Script Name]**\n54: \n55: ### Step C: YouTube Chapters Generation\n56: Whenever generating a timeline for YouTube, calculate relative timestamps starting at `00:00`:\n57: - Format: `MM:SS Song Title`\n58: - First timestamp must start at `00:00`.\n59: - At least 3 timestamps in ascending order.\n60: Provide both:\n61: - Option A: Songs Only (e.g. `00:00 Song 1...`)\n62: - Option B: Full Detail (Songs + Spoken Sharings)\n63: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
